course: dictionary
lesson: 5660
title: Literature: written works worth reading
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Literature means written works such as novels, poems and plays, especially ones people think are good or important. Look at the clues around the word. «His «Kobzar» (1840) is a founding book of modern Ukrainian literature» tells you that literature is a whole body of written work, not just one book.
explain: The context often shows you which meaning is right. «In 1907 he became the first English-language writer to win the Nobel Prize in Literature» is about writing that is honoured with a prize. In a school lesson, English literature means studying stories, poems and plays and what they mean.
explain: In science, «the literature» means everything already published on a topic. Everyday life can use the word for leaflets too. So ask yourself: are the words around it about books and poems, about lessons, about science papers, or about printed information?
fact: Literature means written works such as novels, poems and plays.
fact: Literature can also mean the school or university subject that studies these works.
fact: In science and research, «the literature» means all the writing already published on a topic.
fact: Printed leaflets and booklets are sometimes called literature, as in «free literature about the museum».
fact: Useful phrases: English literature, children's literature, a work of literature.
exercise: «In 1907 he became the first English-language writer to win the Nobel Prize in Literature.» What does literature mean here? | Pictures hung in a gallery | The study of science | *Written works such as novels, poems and plays | Printed leaflets and booklets
exercise: Ravi picks up some free literature about the museum. What does literature mean here? | *Printed leaflets and booklets | Novels and poems | A kind of museum building | Lessons about maths
exercise: In school, English literature lessons study stories, poems and plays. What does English literature mean here? | Painting and drawing in art class | *The study of written works such as stories and plays | Printed leaflets about the library | Learning to swim
test: In the phrase «a work of literature», what does literature mean? | *A written book, poem or play | A science paper about rocks | A school timetable | A printed leaflet
test: Which phrase means all the published writing on a topic? | English literature | *The literature on volcanoes | A work of literature | Children's literature
exam: Which of these is an example of literature? | A weather report | A shopping list | A bus timetable | *A famous poem
